Third-party data notices for tests/data/kblock/
================================================

These fixtures are derived data, committed under this repository for testing
`reblock.data.kblock.KblockSource`. reblock's own code license (see the repo's top-level LICENSE,
if/when added) does NOT apply to the data in this directory — each source below carries its own
license, orthogonal to reblock's code license. See PROVENANCE.md for full source URLs, retrieval
date, checksums, and the exact selection predicate used to produce these fixtures.

1. Google Open Buildings V3 (Cape Town building points)
--------------------------------------------------------

`buildings_capetown_sample.parquet` is derived from Google Research's Open Buildings V3 dataset.

  Copyright Google LLC. Licensed under CC BY 4.0.
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  Dataset: https://sites.research.google/open-buildings/

  Citation:
  Sirko, W., et al. "Continental-Scale Building Detection from High Resolution Satellite Imagery."
  arXiv:2107.12283 (2021).

  Modifications made by this repository:
    - Filtered to the Cape Town bounding box (lon in [18.3, 19.0], lat in [-34.4, -33.5]).
    - Filtered to confidence >= 0.7.
    - Emitted as point (centroid) geometries only, dropping all other source columns except
      `area_in_meters` and `confidence` in the raw download (the committed fixture keeps only
      `geometry`, per the KblockSource building-points interface).
    - Further subset to only the points that spatially join (predicate="within") into one of the
      ~300 densest Cape Town blocks selected for this fixture (see PROVENANCE.md).

2. kblock / Million Neighborhoods Africa Database (block geometries + k_complexity)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`blocks_dji_sample.parquet` and `blocks_capetown_sample.parquet` are derived from the Million
Neighborhoods Africa Database (Mansueto Institute for Urban Innovation, University of Chicago),
distributed via Harvard Dataverse:
https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/DQY54U

  Citation:
  Bettencourt, Luis M. A.; Marchio, Nicholas. (2023). Million Neighborhoods Africa Database.
  University of Chicago. https://www.millionneighborhoods.africa

  LICENSE NOTE (unresolved conflict — flagged, not silently picked): the Dataverse dataset-level
  `license` field reports CC0 1.0, but the dataset's own citation notes state verbatim: "Million
  Neighborhoods Africa Database (2023) is made available under the Open Database License:
  http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/." This repository treats the data as **ODbL 1.0**
  (attribution + share-alike) pending resolution with the depositor, and provides this attribution
  accordingly:

  Million Neighborhoods Africa Database is made available under the Open Database License (ODbL):
  http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. Any rights in individual contents of the database
  are licensed under the Database Contents License: http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/dbcl/1.0/.

  Modifications made by this repository:
    - Subset to a density-selected sample of ~300 blocks per city (+ 1 pinned validation block
      each) out of the full country dataset (see PROVENANCE.md for the exact predicate).
    - Kept only the `block_id`, `k_complexity`, `geometry` columns (dropped ~53 other columns:
      population/urban-hierarchy/street-network fields not used by KblockSource).

