-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`buildings_dji_sample.parquet` is ultimately derived from OpenStreetMap building data (converted to
centroid points by the kblock project and redistributed in its `sample-data.zip` reprex archive;
see PROVENANCE.md for the exact URL and extraction method).

  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors. Licensed under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0.
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/

  Modifications made by this repository:
    - Extracted only the `buildings_points_DJI.parquet` entry from the archive (no other content
      from sample-data.zip is used or redistributed).
    - Further subset to only the points that spatially join (predicate="within") into one of the
      ~300 densest DJI blocks selected for this fixture (see PROVENANCE.md).

